	abstract = {In 2018 UAE Federal Competitiveness and Statistics Centre (FCSC) commenced the development of a modernized geo-spatial road map which started by studying the key attributes to serve national statistics and sustainability. Upon this it launched 1MAP initiative to integrate geographical and statistical data through established governmental data collaboration to support planning, crisis management and decision making as well as to provide the community with authoritative maps and official statistics while leveraging latest geospatial technology and artificial intelligence technologies. 1MAP has 4 main objectives, [1] to establish a a national statistical geospatial framework that integrates geospatial and statistical data to support decision-making to enable national geo-statistics where maps and statistical data are combined to support national decision-making through different dashboards, webmaps and storymaps. [2] To develop foundational administrative and urban maps - which are nationally harmonized and up-to-date. [3]To build a national authoritative data source for different community's facilities like education, health, and cultural, and social welfare facilities through 1MAP Facilities Catalog Module. [4]To implement a national collaborative geographic information portal that collects geospatial data from partners, process, standardize it then create sites and different application to serve the community and governmental partners serving various statistical sectors spatial data.. 1MAP sites serves as 1-stop page to partners with spatial data/apps. To achieve these objectives, data standardization and harmonization workflows takes place to consolidate and develop geodatasets received for the 7 emirates from national and local governments into one national map that serves multi sectors requirements. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
